# Content and Data

## Data-First Structure

- Keep reusable page copy and content objects in `data/`.
- Use `data/*.ts` for plain objects/arrays.
- Use `data/*.tsx` only when content truly needs JSX fragments (for example rich FAQ answers).
- Avoid embedding long repeated text directly in page components.

## Typing Patterns

- Infer mapped-item types from source data where practical.
- Preferred style: `(typeof projects)[number]`.
- Store shared reusable type contracts in `types.ts`.

## Content Consistency

- Preserve Czech-first tone and terminology unless task states otherwise.
- Keep wording consistent across navigation, cards, hero text, and FAQ.
- For regulatory/investment wording, prioritize clarity and trust over hype.

## Link and Asset Content Rules

- Keep downloadable files and static assets in `public/`.
- Ensure all external links use safe attributes when opening new tabs.
- Keep image alt text descriptive and localized to page language.
